% What lesson 1's family tree should say.  A fact must be derived;
% `:- fact.` must never be.
%
% One thing is left unsaid on purpose.  The program's sibling rule is
% lesson 1's deliberate bug (everyone with a parent is their own
% sibling), and `:- sibling(X, X).` would fail.
%
%   python3 diagnose.py programs/family.dl --expect programs/family.expect
%   python3 mutation.py programs/family.dl --expect programs/family.expect

grandparent(abe, carl).
grandparent(abe, dana).
:- grandparent(abe, bob).        % a parent is not a grandparent
sibling(bob, ann).               % abe's children
:- sibling(carl, dana).          % cousins
ancestor(abe, carl).
ancestor(abe, dana).
:- ancestor(carl, abe).          % not the other way round
